// Logical schema and field catalogue for the IMBC platform, Phase 1.
//
// Document responsibilities:
// - docs/technical-specification/specification.md defines functional requirements,
//   ownership, visibility, validation, and acceptance. It does not repeat this catalogue.
// - This DBML owns the complete backend field inventory, relationships, source-column
//   mapping, reference dictionaries, and the standard export contract below.
// - The signed-off workbooks are docs/initial-data/IMBC_Manufacturers_Database.xlsx
//   and docs/initial-data/demand_forecast_detailed_under_NDA.xlsx. The additional LPS
//   source is docs/initial-data/LC LPS table for Platform.xlsx; its value mappings
//   require IMBC review before loading. Spreadsheet columns describe source data,
//   not a requirement for one editable database field per cell.
// - Confirmed field decisions in the 13 November 2026 design review are incorporated.
//   Earlier presentations and architecture field inventories are superseded where
//   they conflict. Section revisions, ownership boundaries, files, and catalog
//   projection follow the architecture unless a newer functional rule requires change.
//
// Storage rules:
// - Primary keys are UUIDv7. Submitted and verified revisions are immutable.
// - profile_section.verified_revision_id is what operators, observers, exports,
//   and the pull API read. pending_revision_id is awaiting SME review.
// - Profile rows carry organization_id. Composite references prevent cross-company
//   relationships. Application validation also checks dictionary kinds, parent-child
//   classifications, same-profile identities, conditional requirements, and ranges.
// - Source refreshes create revisions or audited source snapshots; they never mutate
//   a submitted or verified revision. Manufacturer-owned values remain separate from
//   source-owned legal data. No manufacturer confirmation is required for Adata data.
// - Files are versioned outside domain rows and cannot be opened before scan success.
// - catalog_profile and its facets are rebuilt projections, not sources of truth.
// - LPS is a separate SME-maintained register. Operators and the director read saved,
//   non-deleted entries without manufacturer verification or NDA conditions. No LPS
//   record changes manufacturer data, tiers, due diligence, forecasts, or workflows.
// - Tier, site surveyed, completeness, total headcount, and works-with count are derived.
//   Tier 3 requires an identified product with an AGAR/CDP report-issued-or-later status.
// - Audit, submitted revisions, review decisions, NDA acceptances, confirmations,
//   and works-with changes are append-only. Dates and schedules use Asia/Almaty.
// - The configured identity provider (Keycloak or IMBC OIDC provider) holds credentials
//   and is authoritative for failed sign-ins and temporary lockouts; account columns
//   only mirror its state. Queue internals are outside this schema.
// - Source refreshes and due-diligence replacement atomically append complete before/after
//   record and checklist values to audit_entry; current-state rows never replace history.
//
// Signed-off manufacturer source mapping
// Sheet: 1. IMBC Manufacturers' Data; header row 1; columns A:AL.
// Every original cell, Excel comment, and hyperlink target remains in the restricted
// migration journal. A normalized field is populated only when the meaning and target
// are known. Conflicts and incomplete mappings are import_resolution items, not new
// editable legacy columns. Repeated company values are reconciled once per BIN.
// A  No. / row-number formula -> import_row.excel_row_number; never a business ID.
// B  Manufacturer Name in English -> main_information.name_en (optional supplied alias).
// C  Company name -> main_information.legal_name as migration seed; Adata is authoritative.
// D  BIN -> organization.bin; text, one profile per BIN; invalid values are flagged.
// E  Commodity type -> product_line.commodity_type_id via approved dictionary aliases.
// F  Commodity group -> derived parent of that type; OUT OF / N/A remain flagged raw
//    values and do not become valid A-E categories or cause a row to be discarded.
// G  Region -> production_site.region_id after confirming that it describes production.
// H  Company email -> main_information.contact_email; choose a usable company login
//    separately. Multiple addresses are reviewed; never infer focal-point identity.
// I  Company phone -> main_information.company_phone after format normalization.
// J  Company address -> production_site.address only when its purpose is confirmed.
//    Do not copy an ambiguous address into both legal and production addresses.
// K  Website -> main_information.website.
// L  Company focal point -> contact rows + is_focal_point; parse combined names/details
//    only where unambiguous. Missing roles/phones/emails stay incomplete for review.
// M  TN VED code -> product_line.tn_ved_code; split multiple product/code combinations
//    only with an approved association. Do not assign every code to every product.
// N  Product Classification by Economic Activities (KPVED RK) -> product_line_kpved
//    rows; split valid codes, preserve leading zeros and source names where supplied.
// O  Manufactured goods -> product_line.name_en.
// P  Manufactured goods Rus -> product_line.name_ru.
// Q  Supply to Operators -> validated works_with_mark for explicit NCOC/TCO/KPO names.
//    Other counterparties, contractor claims, and unnamed counts remain IMBC notes;
//    an unnamed count never creates named operator relationships.
// R  Expression of interest (EoI) email sent/resent -> imbc_eoi_email_event.sent_on.
// S  Confirmation of receipt -> imbc_engagement.receipt_confirmed (nullable boolean).
// T  Source -> imbc_engagement_source rows referencing the acquisition_source dictionary.
// U  Response to EoI Email -> imbc_engagement.response (interested / not_interested).
// V  Summary of response to EoI -> imbc_engagement.response_summary.
// W  Ready for site visit? -> imbc_engagement.ready_for_site_visit (nullable boolean).
//    R:W are yellow and annotated Review only. Keep them as internal historical
//    context; they do not create an EOI campaign, account invitation, or visit request.
// X  Site visit conducted -> site_survey_record.result.
// Y  Site visit dates -> visit_started_on / visit_ended_on; separate distinct visits.
//    A yes without a usable date is unresolved. A visit without a signed report does
//    not confer site-surveyed status or tier 2.
// Z  Certificates -> certificate records by normalized type; bare type names are
//    incomplete claims, not verified certificates. Obtain details/files on completion.
// AA Overall ranking -> imbc_note with kind legacy_ranking; no platform rank or score.
// AB Shortlisted for CDP / AGAR + AF Status CDP / AGAR -> agar_cdp_record.status.
//    Yes with no later known stage maps to shortlisted. No/blank is not a workflow
//    stage. A later stage supersedes a shortlist marker; contradictions are flagged.
// AC LC/LPS -> imbc_product_context.programme_id (historical programme labels: LC, LPS).
//    This internal manufacturer context does not create or populate an LPS entry.
// AD Priority commodity for IMBC -> imbc_product_context.priority_id (priority list).
//    Non-priority text such as Internal link stays unresolved; it is not a rank.
// AE Year Added to IMBC Database -> imbc_engagement.added_to_imbc_year; not registration.
// AF Status mapping: Completed - Implementation in Progress -> recommendations_in_progress;
//    Completed - Recommended -> recommendation_issued; Shortlisted - Pre-CDP Stage
//    -> shortlisted. Narrative disengagement / unavailable-SME values require review,
//    with explanation in comment. Do not invent a new achieved milestone from prose.
// AG CDP / AGAR execution (%) -> agar_cdp_record.execution_percent, only after approved
//    scale conversion to 0..100. The source stores 0/1 with General formatting; 1 is
//    ambiguous and must not silently become 1% or 100%. It never determines tier.
//    AB/AF/AG are two platform business values: status and execution percentage.
//    Kind, report, and comment remain part of the same product-specific record.
//    If the assessed product or AGAR/CDP kind is unknown, preserve the source in the
//    import journal until IMBC resolves it. Never mark all company products tier 3.
// AH General comments -> imbc_note with kind general.
// AI Manufacturer folder link -> imbc_engagement.folder_url from the hyperlink target,
//    not the display label Open folder. It is internal and not a platform attachment.
// AJ E-ondiris registration -> main_information.unified_register_registered seed.
// AK E-ondiris first inclusion -> main_information.unified_register_first_inclusion_on seed.
// AL E-ondiris note -> imbc_note with kind registry_review; internal, not a registry field.
//
// Signed-off forecast source mapping and import contract
// Sheet: consolidated; header row 1; columns A:J. Header labels are trimmed.
// A id -> forecast_line.source_id (optional source identifier; generated UUID is separate).
// B KPVED_code -> forecast_line.kpved_code (optional text).
// C KPVED_name -> forecast_line.kpved_name (optional source label; dictionary resolves code).
// D TNVED_code -> forecast_line.tn_ved_code (text, complete code or supplied prefix).
// E FPAL Code -> excluded. Do not persist in forecast data, publish, or use as an identity.
// F Commodity name -> forecast_commodity dictionary entry.
// G sub_commodity_name -> forecast_subcommodity dictionary entry under that commodity.
// H Full Description -> forecast_line.description; IMBC removes operators/projects/brands.
// I Unit of Measure -> forecast_line.unit_id through approved unit aliases.
// J Total Estimated until 2031 -> forecast_line.total_quantity and version.horizon_end_year=2031.
//   A later agreed horizon changes version metadata and the matching import heading,
//   not the quantity field. No annual or operator split is introduced.
// Required source headers: B, C, D, F, G, H, I, and the declared horizon quantity header.
// A may be omitted; E and any other extra fields are ignored. B/C values may be blank.
// Required usable row values: TN VED, commodity, subcommodity, description, unit, quantity.
// A-C are blank in the supplied workbook; do not fabricate source IDs or KPVED values.
// dict_commodity!A:B contains blank commodity IDs and repeated commodity names. Deduplicate
// names into the forecast dictionary; do not create 77,000 dictionary entries or reuse FPAL.
// Forecast commodity/subcommodity is a different hierarchy from manufacturer A-E/type.
// Optional approved forecast_classification rows support A-E/type filters; no crosswalk
// is guessed from spelling, FPAL, or row order. Unmapped rows remain usable in the
// forecast's own hierarchy and are marked unclassified for the optional A-E view.
// Unit aliases are approved explicitly (for example case variants). Ambiguous MT, ST,
// dimensions, and packaging units are never guessed or numerically converted on import.
// Blank required values, unknown codes/units, nonnumeric or negative quantities are
// reported before that row is published. A negative requires correction or explicit
// IMBC acceptance with its source meaning recorded; preserve allowed source values
// in forecast_import_issue.source_values. Zero is a valid explicit quantity; blank is not.
// Do not collapse rows solely because their TN VED code, description, or source ID agrees.
//
// LPS source mapping and one-time migration contract
// Source: docs/initial-data/LC LPS table for Platform.xlsx, Sheet1!A1:S58.
// Header row 1; 57 populated source rows and 57 distinct company labels. Company labels
// are not verified legal identities. The existing source combines some partners, local
// ventures, products, services, and phases; SME review determines identities and scopes.
// A  # -> import_row.raw; Excel row is import_row.excel_row_number. Neither is a business ID.
// B  Company -> lps_company.name. Reuse a company only after identity is established;
//    a local venture can be recorded under its supplied name. No BIN/account is required.
// C  Type -> lps_entry.source_type_id, reusing programme entries LC and LPS. Source counts
//    are LC=41 and LPS=16. LC remains a historical label; the feature and new entries use
//    LPS. These labels do not create separate processes or change status/access rules.
// D  Country -> lps_company_country.country_id, using the country dictionary. Six rows
//    list two countries; Kazakhstan is valid, including 33 Kazakhstan-only rows. Do not
//    infer incorporation, ownership, foreign parent, or partner relationships from this cell.
// E  Commodity -> lps_entry_commodity.commodity_type_id via approved aliases.
// F  Commodity group -> derived A-E parents of those types, checked against the source.
//    Multiple types are allowed; source order is not a crosswalk. Row 29 lists groups C,E
//    in an order that cannot be paired with its types. Conflicts remain migration issues.
//    Services without a matching type remain unclassified until IMBC supplies a valid one.
// G  Product -> lps_entry.scope_description, displayed as Product / service. Preserve the
//    full scope. Split independently managed scopes only after SME confirmation, never
//    by punctuation alone. Do not copy investment or jobs to every resulting entry.
// H  Status -> lps_status dictionary: planning (Planning, 16), in_process (In process, 21),
//    localized (Localized, 14), on_hold (On hold, 6). Counts describe this source only.
//    SME selects any current status directly; there is no transition engine or approval.
// I  Planned launch -> lps_entry.planned_launch. Source has 39 quarters, 5 years,
//    one range (I32: Q4 2027 / Q1 2028), 11 TBD, and one blank (I58). Keep that precision.
// J  Comment -> lps_entry.comment; operator-visible LPS context, not a class C IMBC note.
// K  Investment (USD) -> lps_entry.investment_usd. Store source decimal precision; display
//    two decimals without rounding the stored value. Blank is unknown, not zero.
// L  New jobs -> lps_entry.new_jobs; optional nonnegative integer, blank is not zero.
// M  City + N Region -> paired lps_location rows; region uses the existing dictionary.
//    Rows 4 and 38 each list two city/region pairs. Pair only when confirmed; 13 rows
//    have no location. Never assign every city to every region or infer from name alone.
// O  Focal point(s) + P Role / title -> lps_contact name/title records for this entry.
// Q  Email(s) + R Phone(s) -> lps_contact_email / lps_contact_phone. A contact may have
//    several methods. Source counts differ (row 4: 5 names/5 roles/4 emails/5 phones;
//    row 12: 2/2/5/3). Never zip by position. SME confirms each association, including
//    an explicitly general company contact; unresolved methods stay in the source journal.
//    These people are neither accounts nor the manufacturer profile's single focal point.
// S  Last updated -> lps_entry.last_updated_on, an SME-maintained business date. Preserve
//    source dates (17 September to 6 November 2026), separately from platform updated_at.
//
// Use import_batch.source_kind=lps and the existing restricted import_row/import_resolution
// journal for raw cells and unresolved mappings. Every source row remains accounted for.
// lps_entry.migration_key is a stable dataset/sheet/row/resolved-scope key across trial runs;
// reuse accepted company/entry mappings rather than deduplicating by name or scope text.
// Load only after SME reconciliation; this is migration, not a recurring import/publish UI.
// Missing optional values do not prevent entry creation. Missing company/scope/status or
// ambiguous identity/scope is resolved before loading; other unresolved cells can remain
// blank in the entry while their original text and issue remain available to the SME.
// No entry, account, invitation, review, or notification is created from manufacturer LC flags.
//
// LPS table projection (view only for operators; no export or pull-API contract)
// One row per non-deleted lps_entry joined to its company. Preserve workbook column order
// A:S above, using a display row number for #, Product / service for Product, and LC
// (legacy) for the historical LC Type. Join multi-values within a cell in stable display
// order without multiplying entry rows; show contacts and their methods as aligned groups.
// Dictionary values order by sort_order, then translated label, then code. Locations and
// contacts order by their sort_order then ID; contact methods by sort_order then value.
// Sorting a multi-value column compares its ordered list of scalar sort keys
// lexicographically, retaining the aligned contact/location groups in the displayed row.
// Planned-launch ordering uses earliest then latest possible quarter from parsed bounds
// (a year spans Q1..Q4), not lexical order or a claimed exact launch date. Numbers use
// numeric order, Last updated uses date order, and free text uses displayed text order.
// TBD follows known launch periods; null follows TBD in either direction. Other missing
// values also sort last in either direction. The entry ID is the final tie breaker.
// Dashboard: count distinct entry IDs by status/region/commodity, and distinct company IDs
// overall, using the same filters and deletion rules as the list. An entry with no resolved
// region or commodity group has an Unknown bucket in that dimension. Multi-category
// entries count once per applicable category; category totals are not added to obtain an
// overall count. City/region filters match one location pair; type/group filters match one
// classification. No financial totals.
//
// Standard export contract (logical projection, not a separately editable table)
// Contract version: 2. One row per verified product line; search export and subscription
// use the same order and field set. Dictionaries supply display labels. Multiple values
// use the format in DATA-10; join rows before export so codes/certificates do not multiply
// product rows. A product's selected production site supplies region/city/address.
// 01 bin: organization.bin
// 02 company_name_en: main_information.name_en (blank when no supplied English name)
// 03 company_legal_name: main_information.legal_name (source spelling, no translation)
// 04 production_region: selected production_site.region_id label
// 05 production_city: selected production_site.city
// 06 legal_address: main_information.legal_address
// 07 production_address: selected production_site.address
// 08 website: main_information.website
// 09 company_contact_email: main_information.contact_email (never an account credential)
// 10 company_phone: main_information.company_phone
// 11 focal_point_name; 12 focal_point_position; 13 focal_point_email; 14 focal_point_phone:
//    the verified contact with is_focal_point, from full_name/position/email/phone
// 15 oked_codes: main_information_oked.code (all codes returned by Adata)
// 16 commodity_group: parent of product_line.commodity_type_id
// 17 commodity_type: product_line.commodity_type_id label
// 18 product_name_en: product_line.name_en; 19 product_name_ru: product_line.name_ru
// 20 tn_ved_code: product_line.tn_ved_code
// 21 kpved_codes: product_line_kpved.code, one value per code
// 22 production_capacity: capacity_quantity + capacity_unit_id label, or capacity_text
//    from e-Ondiris; the display does not silently convert source units
// 23 workshop_count: production.workshop_count; 24 utilisation_percent: production.utilisation_percent
// 25 total_headcount: sum of personnel.managers_count/engineers_count/production_workers_count
// 26 certificates: valid verified held certificate type + expiry date pairs; absence
//    declarations and missing/unverified claims are not reported as held certificates
// 27 site_surveyed; 28 last_site_visit_on; 29 profile_tier; 30 product_tier_3;
// 31 unified_register_registered; 32 works_with_major_count; 33 verified_at;
// 34 due_diligence_checked_on; 35 pending_changes: corresponding catalog projections
// The API exposes the wider authorized company-page model, including product details,
// sites, held certificates and their files; this compact file contract does not define
// the API response shape. IMBC-only context, operator names/notes, pending values, and
// confidential AGAR reports are excluded from every operator data channel.

Project imbc_platform {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: 'Authoritative Phase 1 backend field catalogue, reconciled with the signed-off manufacturer and detailed-demand workbooks, the additional LPS source workbook, and confirmed field decisions of 13 November 2026. Functional behavior and access remain governed by specification.md. Source mappings and standard export contract are documented above; Excel column count does not dictate database column count.'
}

